NAME
       getenforce - print the current SELinux mode

SYNOPSIS
       getenforce

DESCRIPTION
       getenforce prints Enforcing, Permissive or Disabled.

       Enforcing
              SELinux blocks and logs what the policy does not allow.

       Permissive
              It only logs (useful to test whether SELinux is the cause of
              a problem).

       Disabled
              SELinux is off.

       setenforce 0 or 1 switches between permissive and enforcing until the
       next boot. The mode at boot is SELINUX= in /etc/selinux/config;
       sestatus shows both.

EXAMPLES
           getenforce
           setenforce 1
           grep ^SELINUX= /etc/selinux/config

SEE ALSO
       setenforce(8), sestatus(8), selinux(8)
